      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceCANProtocol_1a88802da4205140719f9714cb416f1b2c" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void CANProtocol::start</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>start</name>
        <qualifiedname>CANProtocol::start</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Start the CAN peripheral and apply registered filters. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Must be called after <ref refid="namespaceSTM32Board_1a3785a13cc5ed58de231b71fd5e143f00" kindref="member">STM32Board::begin()</ref> and after all filter and callback registrations. Always adds CTRL_BCAST, TEST_SEQ, and SYNC_REQ to the active filter — mandatory for all nodes, cannot be excluded — plus HB_0 on every node except <ref refid="namespacePanelBridge" kindref="compound">PanelBridge</ref> (NODE_ID 0), for <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1aee035f550086e47e9c533b9f547687f9" kindref="member">serviceNodeStatus()</ref>&apos;s master-loss watchdog, and the node&apos;s own <computeroutput>HB_NODE_ID</computeroutput>, for its duplicate NODE_ID check (#344).</para>
<para>Resets the <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1aee035f550086e47e9c533b9f547687f9" kindref="member">serviceNodeStatus()</ref> timers, which arm on its first call. Fires the onStatusChange callback with NORMAL on success. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" line="271" column="6" bodyfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" bodystart="271" bodyend="282" declfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.h" declline="269" declcolumn="10"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceCANProtocol_1acc6510e0de85e6bf717989ef8c04cf77" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void CANProtocol::startLoopback</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>startLoopback</name>
        <qualifiedname>CANProtocol::startLoopback</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Start in silent loopback mode — for bench testing only. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Identical to <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1a88802da4205140719f9714cb416f1b2c" kindref="member">start()</ref> but uses CAN_MODE_SILENT_LOOPBACK: frames transmitted by this node are received back internally without going on the physical bus. The duplicate NODE_ID check discounts the node&apos;s own looped-back heartbeats, so only an extra <computeroutput>HB_NODE_ID</computeroutput> a test sends itself reads as a duplicate.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Never call this in production firmware. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" line="283" column="6" bodyfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" bodystart="283" bodyend="283" declfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.h" declline="281" declcolumn="10"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceCANProtocol_1a3215742dd9da68b125f121c95425e2e4" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void CANProtocol::drain</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>drain</name>
        <qualifiedname>CANProtocol::drain</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Process RX callbacks and batched-ControlPacket deadlines. Call once per loop(). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Drains all frames received since the last call:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>SYNC_REQ: fires <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1a8ea19c74f3b784a3844f0e5a1b8ed699" kindref="member">onSyncReq()</ref>, not forwarded to <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1ab9d0d6bb169c659d369e630d1630c0e1" kindref="member">onReceive()</ref>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>TEST_SEQ: auto-replies with ECHO carrying the same payload, not forwarded.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>HB_0 on a non-bridge node: stamped for <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1aee035f550086e47e9c533b9f547687f9" kindref="member">serviceNodeStatus()</ref>&apos;s watchdog, then <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1ab9d0d6bb169c659d369e630d1630c0e1" kindref="member">onReceive()</ref>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The node&apos;s own <computeroutput>HB_NODE_ID</computeroutput>: stamped for <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1aee035f550086e47e9c533b9f547687f9" kindref="member">serviceNodeStatus()</ref>&apos;s duplicate NODE_ID check (#344), then <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1ab9d0d6bb169c659d369e630d1630c0e1" kindref="member">onReceive()</ref>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>The node&apos;s own <computeroutput>BOOT_CMD_n</computeroutput> (not on the bridge): a CONNECT resets into the bootloader when one is installed (<ref refid="namespaceSTM32Board_1a593f38c0e9fea1a50face7d548a9218b" kindref="member">STM32Board::enterBootloader()</ref>, #365); never forwarded.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>All other frames: fires <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1ab9d0d6bb169c659d369e630d1630c0e1" kindref="member">onReceive()</ref>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Also services <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1af4ff9a2b592e08b02306c70bd59e83a9" kindref="member">sendBatched()</ref> deadlines: a half-full ControlPacketPair that has waited two <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1a3215742dd9da68b125f121c95425e2e4" kindref="member">drain()</ref> calls is flushed with slot B set to the null sentinel. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" line="285" column="6" bodyfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" bodystart="285" bodyend="350" declfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.h" declline="299" declcolumn="10"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceCANProtocol_1a2fc92ed4733eeb74630589631e2caf84" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void CANProtocol::send</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint32_t canId, const uint8_t *data, uint8_t len)</argsstring>
        <name>send</name>
        <qualifiedname>CANProtocol::send</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>canId</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>data</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>len</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Send a CAN frame. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Sends immediately if a TX mailbox is free; otherwise enqueues in the TX ring buffer (~16 entries), drained automatically via TX-complete interrupt. CTRL_BCAST coalesces stale queued state (newest wins). EVT/control frames retry up to 3 attempts then drop. All drops increment <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1a1fed615c5c046e667216ff9da46bca91" kindref="member">txDropCount()</ref>.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>canId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>11-bit standard CAN ID. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to payload bytes. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>len</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Payload length in bytes (0-8). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" line="352" column="6" bodyfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" bodystart="352" bodyend="398" declfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.h" declline="315" declcolumn="10"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceCANProtocol_1af4ff9a2b592e08b02306c70bd59e83a9" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void CANProtocol::sendBatched</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint32_t canId, const ControlPacket &amp;pkt)</argsstring>
        <name>sendBatched</name>
        <qualifiedname>CANProtocol::sendBatched</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>canId</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const ControlPacket &amp;</type>
          <declname>pkt</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Submit one ControlPacket to a CANProtocol-owned ControlPacketPair batch. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Valid only for CAN_ID_CTRL_BCAST and the batched event frames — canIdEvt(n) (absolute), canIdEvtRel(n) (RotaryEncoder REL), canIdEvtDir(n) (RotaryEncoder DIR), and canIdEvtAction(n) (ActionButton) — each with its own pending slot. Pairs two consecutive packets into one 8-byte frame. If slot B does not arrive within two <ref refid="namespaceCANProtocol_1a3215742dd9da68b125f121c95425e2e4" kindref="member">drain()</ref> calls, slot A is sent with slot B set to the null sentinel (controlId == 0x0000).</para>
<para>A frame ID with no batch slot is <bold>silently discarded</bold> — adding a batched frame means registering it in _batches[] in begin(), not just defining its canId helper.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>canId</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CAN_ID_CTRL_BCAST, canIdEvt(NODE_ID), canIdEvtRel(NODE_ID), canIdEvtDir(NODE_ID), or canIdEvtAction(NODE_ID). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>pkt</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>ControlPacket to batch. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" line="400" column="6" bodyfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.cpp" bodystart="400" bodyend="419" declfile="Firmware/Libraries/CANProtocol/CANProtocol.h" declline="333" declcolumn="10"/>
      </memberdef>
